+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site. Run `npm test` for the automated WebMCP checks (no browser required).
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The homepage progressively registers three client-side tools through `document.modelContext.registerTool`:
+
+| Tool | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_favorites` | Returns the coffee names, descriptions, and destination IDs shown on the page. |
+| `list_site_destinations` | Returns the IDs, labels, and URLs of explicitly marked homepage links. |
+| `navigate_to_destination` | Accepts `{ "destination": "menu" }` and follows that link in the current tab. |
+
+Read tools accept `{}`. Navigation accepts only the IDs of same-origin links marked with `data-tool-destination`. Logout is deliberately unmarked. Product data comes directly from the visible cards. Tools return JSON-serializable objects, including actionable errors for invalid arguments.
+
+Use HTTPS or a trustworthy localhost origin and a browser with the WebMCP API enabled. Unsupported browsers keep the ordinary page behavior; no polyfill or server transport is installed. Registrations use an AbortSignal for cleanup on `pagehide` and are restored after back/forward cache navigation.
+
+Navigation mirrors the existing links. This static application does not implement the linked routes, an ordering backend, or account operations; the tools do not claim to complete purchases or other transactions.
+
+API reference: [Chrome WebMCP Imperative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
